 seconds, Event: Ball passed to USA player for three-point attempt, score USA 39-AUS 31, 2nd quarter 5:49 remaining",\n        "Time: 2850 seconds, Event: USA player releases three-point shot, crowd standing with arms raised in anticipation, score USA 42-AUS 33, 2nd quarter 5:13 remaining",\n        "Time: 2900 seconds, Event: Three-point shot goes in, USA players celebrate, Australian players disappointed, score USA 44-AUS 34, 2nd quarter 4:58 remaining",\n        "Time: 2950 seconds, Event: Australian coach gives instructions during timeout, players listening, score USA 44-AUS 36, 2nd quarter 4:51 remaining",\n        "Time: 3000 seconds, Event: Play resumes with Australia on offense, score USA 44-AUS 36, 2nd quarter 4:51 remaining"\n    ]\n}\n```'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Successfully recorded 7 event(s). You now have 7 total recorded events. Use VIEW_RECORDS to see all of them sorted by time.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Based on the VLM observations from frames 2714-3000 (which correspond to approximately 45:14-50:00), I can see that the fans are excited because of the intense basketball action during this period. The key events include:\n\n1. A USA player making a three-point shot (frames 2800-2850)\n2. Fast-paced scoring with both teams exchanging points\n3. The competitive nature of the Olympic quarter-final match\n4. Visible crowd reactions including standing, cheering, and waving flags\n\nThe VLM specifically notes that the crowd is excited due to:\n- "A star-level three-point shot under pressure"\n- "Rapid scoring swings" \n- "High-stakes Olympic quarter-final"\n- "Visible coaching drama"\n\nLooking at the answer choices:\nA. Because they are genuinely happy - Too vague\nB. Because both teams performed very well - Supported by evidence of both teams scoring\nC. Because Australian National Team performed very well - Only partially true\nD. Because United States National Team performed very well - Only partially true\n\nThe evidence shows bo